WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.480 --> 00:00:06.450
How big of a role does your age play when
it comes to entrepreneurship?

00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:07.450
Think about that.

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:12.080
That is probably one of the most common questions
I get asked all the time.

00:00:12.080 --> 00:00:16.730
On Snapchat, on Facebook, on Cyberdust, on
Twitter - Pat, I'm 18 years old, how old do

00:00:16.730 --> 00:00:17.820
I need to be to be an entrepreneur?

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.789
Hey Pat, do you think I can still be a strong
entrepreneur?

00:00:20.789 --> 00:00:21.789
I'm only this age.

00:00:21.789 --> 00:00:22.789
I'm only that age.

00:00:22.789 --> 00:00:23.789
What is a good age?

00:00:23.789 --> 00:00:30.869
So today I want to us to process if you can
be a good entrepreneur and a successful entrepreneur

00:00:30.869 --> 00:00:36.000
being young, whatever age you are, and what
are real benefits of being an older entrepreneur

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:37.000
vs. a younger entrepreneur.

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:41.840
And then at the end I'll give you some of
the stereotypes younger entrepreneurs get

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:44.460
that's going to be your enemy if you're watching
this, and you're younger.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:48.129
Your enemy is going to be these few things
I talk to you about and then we'll go from

00:00:48.129 --> 00:00:49.129
there.

00:00:49.129 --> 00:00:50.129
So here's what it is.

00:00:50.129 --> 00:00:54.719
An older entrepreneur vs. a younger entrepreneur
-- does age really matter?

00:00:54.719 --> 00:00:57.059
Older people are typically more paranoid.

00:00:57.059 --> 00:01:01.340
That helps in business because when you're
older, people have stolen from you, lied to

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:05.750
you, given you some deals that didn't go through,
a bad partnership, bad relationship, so you're

00:01:05.750 --> 00:01:08.730
paranoia is higher, and that typically helps
in business.

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:11.370
When you're younger, you're more naive.

00:01:11.370 --> 00:01:18.550
You think the world is a great place, you
believe world peace exists and everything

00:01:18.550 --> 00:01:21.400
can be nirvana and utopia exists, all this
stuff.

00:01:21.400 --> 00:01:22.400
Not fully.

00:01:22.400 --> 00:01:23.400
I'm not saying everybody.

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:27.900
Because there are some kids that grew up in
some cities -- if you grow up in Boston and

00:01:27.900 --> 00:01:33.580
L.A. and South side Chicago - if you grew
up in some places, New York, Bronx, some places

00:01:33.580 --> 00:01:37.850
you grow up, you're going to learn about being
bullied and pushed around so you'll have that.

00:01:37.850 --> 00:01:40.790
But generally, younger is going to be more
naive.

00:01:40.790 --> 00:01:41.790
Older is going to be wiser.

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:43.090
They've had more mistakes.

00:01:43.090 --> 00:01:44.690
They've seen things.

00:01:44.690 --> 00:01:46.470
Younger think they know it all.

00:01:46.470 --> 00:01:47.670
Right?They think they know everything.

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:48.670
Totally fine.

00:01:48.670 --> 00:01:50.119
Stay with me.

00:01:50.119 --> 00:01:52.340
Older have more contacts.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:54.720
Younger it's really only family, friends,
and teachers.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:56.320
But older they have a lot more contacts.

00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:58.720
Older is more logical.

00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:00.360
Younger is more emotional.

00:02:00.360 --> 00:02:02.220
Older have lots to lose.

00:02:02.220 --> 00:02:05.160
So the decision making process is different.

00:02:05.160 --> 00:02:06.860
Younger they have nothing to lose, right?

00:02:06.860 --> 00:02:12.250
So when you ask the question who is more capable,
you have to look at these things.

00:02:12.250 --> 00:02:15.000
And by the way, there's a lot more things
I can add to this list but I want to keep

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.000
this video very, very simple.

00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:21.019
But I want you to think about it in a completely
opposite way.

00:02:21.019 --> 00:02:25.409
So right now the way that I'm explaining it,
it's more beneficial to be older and be an

00:02:25.409 --> 00:02:26.489
entrepreneur, right?

00:02:26.489 --> 00:02:28.049
Well, is it really?

00:02:28.049 --> 00:02:29.969
Because think about this.

00:02:29.969 --> 00:02:36.459
There is some level of naiveness that's actually
not bad for business.

00:02:36.459 --> 00:02:37.459
Why?

00:02:37.459 --> 00:02:43.790
Because there's a certain level of optimism
to think that people are going to help you.

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:46.239
So you're willing to ask people for help.

00:02:46.239 --> 00:02:48.030
Where this person is like, "oh, they'll never
help us.

00:02:48.030 --> 00:02:49.299
Oh, they won't be interested.

00:02:49.299 --> 00:02:50.349
They won't want to do anything."

00:02:50.349 --> 00:02:52.749
You're [the younger] are like, "They will
help us!

00:02:52.749 --> 00:02:54.670
Why wouldn't they help us!

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:55.969
Of course they'd love to team up!

00:02:55.969 --> 00:02:58.260
Who wouldn't want to do something like that."

00:02:58.260 --> 00:03:02.859
That's the child-like naiveness that's necessary
for business.

00:03:02.859 --> 00:03:07.030
While this person [the older] is wiser, and
you [younger] think you know it all, right?

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:08.689
The younger generation may think they know
it all.

00:03:08.689 --> 00:03:13.810
"Oh, you know what, sometimes these younger
people, they think they know everything!"

00:03:13.810 --> 00:03:18.629
Is it really that they think they know everything,
or is it really something that they think

00:03:18.629 --> 00:03:21.280
everything is possible?

00:03:21.280 --> 00:03:24.730
Because I don't think it's really the younger
generation thinks they know it all.

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:27.049
They just think it's more possible.

00:03:27.049 --> 00:03:29.969
Now, this notion we always hear about is what?

00:03:29.969 --> 00:03:31.510
They think they know it all.

00:03:31.510 --> 00:03:32.510
They're clueless.

00:03:32.510 --> 00:03:33.510
They're kids.

00:03:33.510 --> 00:03:35.219
No, no, no, no, no.

00:03:35.219 --> 00:03:40.010
What you're really saying is you don't believe
it's possible and they think it's possible.

00:03:40.010 --> 00:03:44.760
Maybe the older entrepreneur and the older
generation needs a little bit more of possibility

00:03:44.760 --> 00:03:47.469
thinking that the [younger] inject into us.

00:03:47.469 --> 00:03:49.420
Next one, contacts.

00:03:49.420 --> 00:03:52.530
They [older] have more leverage for contacts.

00:03:52.530 --> 00:03:54.069
You [younger] don't have that many contacts.

00:03:54.069 --> 00:03:56.989
That part is absolutely true.

00:03:56.989 --> 00:04:04.519
However, older people again, are more reluctant
to ask for help than younger people are.

00:04:04.519 --> 00:04:05.519
The younger don't care.

00:04:05.519 --> 00:04:13.879
By the way, if you're watching this right
now, and you are under the age of 23, 24,

00:04:13.879 --> 00:04:18.540
25, and you have teachers, professors, coaches
that like you, family members, uncles who

00:04:18.540 --> 00:04:24.630
like you -- let me tell you what script will
work for you, pretty much 60 - 70% of the

00:04:24.630 --> 00:04:25.630
time.

00:04:25.630 --> 00:04:26.630
Are you ready?

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:27.730
I need your help.

00:04:27.730 --> 00:04:29.390
Done deal.

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:30.390
I need your help.

00:04:30.390 --> 00:04:31.600
Auntie, I need your help.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:32.600
Mom, I need your help.

00:04:32.600 --> 00:04:33.600
Dad, I need your help.

00:04:33.600 --> 00:04:35.220
Hey coach, I need your help.

00:04:35.220 --> 00:04:37.220
Hey, teacher, I need your help.

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:39.320
Hey, counselor, I need your help.

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:42.220
Hey, you played such a big role in my life,
